{
  "protocol": "coap",
  "title": "CoAP",
  "source": "RFC 7252",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "coap",
      "kind": "protocol",
      "as": "CoAP",
      "about": [
        "RFC 7252 §3 Figure 7 gives one message format, and what a message IS — a request, a response, an",
        "acknowledgement — is the Type and Code fields inside it rather than a different layout. So one message",
        "here, like DHCP and unlike MQTT.",
        "",
        "WHAT MAKES CoAP CoAP is the option encoding, and it is unlike TCP's or DHCP's in one specific way: an",
        "option does not carry its own number. §3.1 gives the DELTA from the previous option, so option N is",
        "only knowable from options 0..N-1, and the same octets mean different options depending on what came",
        "before them. Going out that means the delta is worked out from the list — each item's number less the",
        "one before it, which is why the calculation reads the whole list and its own place in it. Coming in it",
        "means the deltas are what there is, and turning them back into numbers is a sum the reader keeps.",
        "",
        "AND BOTH NIBBLES ESCAPE. Thirteen means an octet follows holding the value less thirteen; fourteen",
        "means two octets follow holding it less 269; fifteen is not a value at all — it marks the payload. So",
        "one nibble decides whether the next octet is part of this option or the start of the next one.",
        "",
        "WHERE THE OPTIONS END is therefore not something a count says, and not something the octets running",
        "out says either: a message with a payload ends its options at a 0xFF that would otherwise read as an",
        "option header of fifteen and fifteen. The reading looks at the next octet before deciding whether it",
        "is about to read another option — which is `identifies` doing at a fork inside a message what it does",
        "at the top of MQTT."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "coapMessage",
      "kind": "message",
      "as": "CoAP message"
    },
    {
      "id": "packing.coapMessage",
      "kind": "packing",
      "as": "the one arrangement"
    },
    {
      "id": "header",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the fixed header",
      "about": "RFC 7252 §3: version, type, token length, code and message id — four octets before anything varies."
    },
    {
      "id": "version",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Ver",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 2
      },
      "about": "§3: 1, and a message with any other is ignored."
    },
    {
      "id": "type",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "T",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 2
      },
      "about": "§3: 0 Confirmable, 1 Non-confirmable, 2 Acknowledgement, 3 Reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "tokenLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "TKL",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 4
      },
      "about": [
        "§3: how many octets of token follow, 0 to 8. Not supplied — it is the length of the token itself, so",
        "the two cannot disagree, and a message where they do is one that reads the first option as a token."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "code",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "Code",
      "about": "§12.1.1: three bits of class and five of detail, which is why a response is written 2.05 rather than as the number 69."
    },
    {
      "id": "codeClass",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "class",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 3
      },
      "about": "§12.1.1: 0 is a request, 2 success, 4 client error, 5 server error."
    },
    {
      "id": "codeDetail",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "detail",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "messageId",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Message ID",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "§3: what pairs an acknowledgement with what it acknowledges."
    },
    {
      "id": "token",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Token",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "about": [
        "§5.3.1: what pairs a response with its request, chosen by whoever sends the request. Zero to eight",
        "octets, and genuinely absent at zero rather than present and empty — the third capture has none."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "input.type",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "T",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "§3: 0 Confirmable, 1 Non-confirmable, 2 Acknowledgement, 3 Reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.codeClass",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "class",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "§12.1.1: the class of the code."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.codeDetail",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "detail",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "§12.1.1: the detail of the code."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.messageId",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Message ID",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "§3."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.token",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Token",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "purpose": "§5.3.1: zero to eight octets. Empty means the message carries no token at all."
    },
    {
      "id": "constant.version",
      "kind": "constant",
      "label": "1, which is this version of CoAP",
      "holds": {
        "int": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.tokenLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of token",
      "runs": "len(token)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "token": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasToken",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "was a token given?",
      "runs": "len(token) > 0",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "token": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.tokenThere",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "does the token length say there is one?",
      "runs": "tkl > 0",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "tkl": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.tokenExtent",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of token, from the length",
      "runs": "tkl",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "tkl": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "options",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "Options",
      "about": [
        "How many there are is nowhere in the message, so going out this is written once per item of the list",
        "it requires and coming in the reading goes round. Same shape as TCP's options and DHCP's — what is",
        "different is that an option here does not say which option it is."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "option",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "an option",
      "about": [
        "§3.1: a nibble of delta and a nibble of length, then whichever extensions those nibbles asked for,",
        "then the value. The extensions are separate fields rather than one span of computed width because the",
        "RFC gives them as separate cases — 'an 8-bit unsigned integer follows' and 'a 16-bit unsigned integer",
        "in network byte order follows' — and they are read and written as those."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "optionDeltaNibble",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Delta",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 4
      },
      "about": "§3.1: 0..12 is the delta itself; 13 and 14 say an extension follows; 15 is reserved and is what the payload marker's upper nibble looks like."
    },
    {
      "id": "optionLengthNibble",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "optionDeltaExt8",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Delta (extended)",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "§3.1: the delta less 13."
    },
    {
      "id": "optionDeltaExt16",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Delta (extended)",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "§3.1: the delta less 269."
    },
    {
      "id": "optionLengthExt8",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Length (extended)",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "§3.1: the length less 13."
    },
    {
      "id": "optionLengthExt16",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Length (extended)",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "§3.1: the length less 269."
    },
    {
      "id": "optionValue",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Option Value",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "about": [
        "Whatever the option carries, kept as octets. What a Uri-Path means is a fact about option 11 rather",
        "than about the shape of an option, and this describes the shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "input.options",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Options",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": {
        "number": "Int",
        "value": "Bytes"
      },
      "purpose": "The options to write, in ascending order of number. Each says its `number` — the option number RFC 7252 §5.10 assigns, not the delta — and its `value` as octets."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.delta",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "how far past the previous option this one is",
      "runs": "item.number - (ordinal == 0 ? 0 : index(options, ordinal - 1).number)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "options": "List"
      },
      "about": [
        "§3.1: 'The Option Numbers are calculated by summing the Option Delta values'. Going out that",
        "is a subtraction, and it needs the option before this one — which is why this reads the whole",
        "list and its own place in it rather than just its own item.",
        "",
        "It is also the reason an option cannot be described on its own: the same octets are a",
        "different option depending on what preceded them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.length",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of value",
      "runs": "len(item.value)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "about": [
        "From the ITEM rather than from the field it becomes, and that is not a shortcut. Whether an extension",
        "is there depends on this, and presence has to settle before the walk can go on — so taking it from a",
        "field the walk has not reached yet asks for a fact about a place nothing has arrived at. The length is",
        "a fact about the value the caller supplied, and saying so directly is both true and answerable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.deltaNibble",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the delta, or which escape it needs",
      "runs": "delta < 13 ? delta : (delta < 269 ? 13 : 14)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "delta": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.deltaExt8",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the delta less thirteen",
      "runs": "delta - 13",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "delta": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasDeltaExt8",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "does the nibble say an octet follows?",
      "runs": "nibble == 13",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "nibble": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.deltaExt16",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the delta less 269",
      "runs": "delta - 269",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "delta": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasDeltaExt16",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "does the nibble say two octets follow?",
      "runs": "nibble == 14",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "nibble": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.lengthNibble",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the length, or which escape it needs",
      "runs": "length < 13 ? length : (length < 269 ? 13 : 14)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "length": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.lengthExt8",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the length less thirteen",
      "runs": "length - 13",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "length": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasLengthExt8",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "does the nibble say an octet follows?",
      "runs": "nibble == 13",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "nibble": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.lengthExt16",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the length less 269",
      "runs": "length - 269",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "length": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasLengthExt16",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "does the nibble say two octets follow?",
      "runs": "nibble == 14",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "nibble": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.eachValue",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this option's value",
      "runs": "item.value",
      "gives": "Bytes"
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.valueExtent",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of value, from the nibble and whatever followed it",
      "runs": "nibble < 13 ? nibble : (nibble == 13 ? ext8 + 13 : ext16 + 269)",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "nibble": "Int",
        "ext8": "Int",
        "ext16": "Int"
      },
      "about": [
        "Only the branch the nibble picks is worked out, which is what lets this name all three: an",
        "extension that is not there has no value, and asking for one would be asking about an octet the",
        "message does not contain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "optionMore",
      "kind": "junction",
      "as": "is there anything left?"
    },
    {
      "id": "optionWhich",
      "kind": "junction",
      "as": "another option, or the payload?",
      "about": [
        "The fork the whole reading turns on. A message whose options run to the end of the datagram simply",
        "runs out; one with a payload ends them at a 0xFF, which as an option header would read as a delta of",
        "fifteen — and §3.1 says fifteen is not a delta. So the reading looks at the octet before deciding",
        "whether it is about to read an option at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "probe.optionHeader",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "the next octet",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": [
        "Read from a copy of the position and consumed from nothing. Whichever way it picks then reads the",
        "same octet properly — as two nibbles if it is an option, as the payload marker if it is 0xFF."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.anythingLeft",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "are there octets left?",
      "runs": "remaining > 0",
      "gives": "Bool"
    },
    {
      "id": "payloadMarker",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "the payload marker",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": [
        "§3: 0xFF, present if and only if there is a payload. A marker with nothing after it is a message",
        "format error rather than an empty payload — which is the same law as an omitted default: one thing,",
        "one encoding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "payload",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Payload",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "about": [
        "Everything left. §3: 'The payload ... extends to the end of the datagram', so nothing measures it and",
        "nothing needs to — how long it is, is a fact about the datagram rather than about CoAP."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "input.payload",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Payload",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "purpose": "The payload octets, or empty for a message that carries none."
    },
    {
      "id": "constant.payloadMarker",
      "kind": "constant",
      "label": "0xFF",
      "holds": {
        "int": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "constant.yes",
      "kind": "constant",
      "label": "yes",
      "holds": {
        "bool": true
      },
      "about": "Coming in, arriving here IS the answer: the reading only takes this way on having looked at the octet and found the marker. Going out it is the caller's payload that decides."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasPayloadMarker",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "is there a payload?",
      "runs": "len(payload) > 0",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "payload": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.hasPayload",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "is there a payload?",
      "runs": "len(payload) > 0",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "payload": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "done",
      "kind": "end-parse",
      "as": "the end of a CoAP message"
    },
    {
      "id": "validator.version",
      "kind": "validator",
      "because": "§3: the version is 1.",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 1
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "validator.tokenLength",
      "kind": "validator",
      "because": "§3: \"Lengths 9-15 are reserved ... and MUST be processed as a message format error\".",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 0
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 8
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
